course: dictionary
lesson: 12291
title: Conveyance, a word with three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A conveyance is a way of carrying people or things from one place to another. «The old horse-drawn conveyance rattled down the lane.» Here it means a vehicle, a carriage pulled by a horse. Ask yourself what is being carried, then check that your meaning still fits the sentence.
explain: Conveyance can also mean the act of carrying or moving something. «The conveyance of water through the plant's stem keeps its leaves green.» No vehicle is mentioned. The clues "of water" and "through the stem" show that the word means moving water from one place to another.
explain: Lawyers use the word in a special way. «The lawyer handled the conveyance when the family bought their house.» Here it means the legal work of passing ownership of a house or land to someone new. Phrases like «means of conveyance» and «public conveyance» are set phrases, so learn them as a group.
fact: A conveyance is a vehicle or any way of carrying people or things.
fact: Conveyance can also mean the act of carrying or moving something from one place to another.
fact: Conveyancing is the legal work of passing ownership of a house or land to someone else.
fact: «Conveyance» is a formal word, used more in serious or old-fashioned writing than in everyday talk.
fact: «Means of conveyance» means a way of travelling or carrying things, and «public conveyance» means a bus, train or other vehicle that anyone can use.
exercise: «The horse-drawn conveyance rolled slowly into town.» What is a conveyance here? | *A carriage or vehicle | A kind of weather | A type of bread | A sad song
exercise: «The conveyance of water through the plant kept every leaf green.» What does conveyance mean here? | *Carrying water from one place to another | Drying the water up | A wet, grey day | A pretty flower
exercise: «Buses and trains are public conveyances.» Which of these is a public conveyance? | A sunny day | A cloud | *A bus | A loaf of bread
test: «When a lawyer does the conveyance of a house, what is she doing?» | Painting the walls of the house | *Handling the legal work of passing ownership to a new owner | Cleaning the windows and garden | Moving the furniture into a van
test: «Ella used a means of conveyance to get to school.» What does means of conveyance mean? | A school rule about lunch | A kind of cake | A map of the town | *A way of travelling, such as a bus or bike
exam: «The conveyance of goods across the sea took three weeks.» What does conveyance mean here? | A type of cloud | A small boat for fishing | *The carrying of goods from one place to another | A legal contract for a house
